{"ts": 1789777832.193409, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "I'll go with **{16, 3, 32}, all long** (IS Sharpe 1.053).\n\nReasoning on the OOS prediction:\n\n- **Feature 16 and 3** are the two genuinely reliable legs \u2014 standalone Sharpes of 0.71 and 0.66, each ~3\u03c3 above the ~0.22 noise floor. These were picked from 40 candidates, so even they carry some selection bias; shrinking a 0.7 max-of-40 toward the mean suggests true values nearer 0.5\u20130.6.\n- **Feature 32** was chosen as the best of ~26 tested third legs that all clustered in 0.85\u20131.05. Its marginal contribution (+0.08) is well within the noise band, and near-zero-signal features gave nearly as much lift. I expect most of that +0.08 to evaporate; 32's own standalone 0.455 is only ~2\u03c3, so it likely contributes something, just less than measured.\n- **Selection bias overall**: I ran ~70 evaluations and am reporting the maximum. The optimism on the top-line 1.05 is meaningful. A reasonable decomposition: the two-feature core is worth ~0.75\u20130.85 OOS, and the third leg adds ~0.0\u20130.05 in expectation.\n\nI'll center my belief at **0.82** with an SD of **0.25** \u2014 the SD reflects both estimation error (~0.22 at this sample size) and the risk that any regime shift degrades these relationships further."}
