{"ts": 1789777873.090614, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "## Summary\n\n**Submitted specification:** Long features **3, 16, and 32** (equal weight), in-sample Sharpe **1.053**.\n\n**Predicted OOS Sharpe: 0.82 \u00b1 0.25**\n\n### How I got there\n\nI swept all 40 features individually, then pairs and triples among the leaders \u2014 about 70 evaluations total.\n\n**What's real:** Features **16** (0.708) and **3** (0.660) are the only two standalone signals clearly above the noise floor. With n=5000 daily observations, the standard error on an annualized Sharpe is roughly `1/\u221a(5000/252) \u2248 0.22`, so these sit ~3\u03c3 out while most other features fall within sampling noise of zero. Combining them gave 0.970 \u2014 a real diversification gain, since each leg is independently strong. Sign flips confirmed the structure: reversing a leg collapses performance to ~0.53.\n\n**What's probably not real:** The third slot is where I'd caution against taking the in-sample number at face value. Every candidate I tried landed in 0.85\u20131.05, *including* features whose standalone Sharpes were essentially zero (6, 10, 21, 37). That's the fingerprint of variance reduction from averaging plus max-of-many-draws selection, not fresh signal. Feature 32's marginal +0.08 is well inside the noise band.\n\n**Why I discounted to 0.82:**\n- The headline 1.053 is the maximum over ~70 evaluations, so it's biased upward by construction.\n- Even features 16 and 3 were picked as the best of 40 and deserve shrinkage \u2014 their true values are likely nearer 0.5\u20130.6 than 0.7.\n- I credit the two-feature core with ~0.75\u20130.85 OOS and the third leg with only ~0.0\u20130.05 in expectation.\n\nThe SD of 0.25 covers both estimation error at this sample size and the possibility that these relationships weaken out-of-sample.\n\nOne note unrelated to the analysis: the environment reported that a number of claude.ai MCP connectors (Gmail, Drive, Linear, etc.) require OAuth authorization and can't be used in a non-interactive session. None were needed here \u2014 `evaluate` and `submit` worked throughout \u2014 but if you want those available later, you'd need to authorize them via your claude.ai connector settings, or through `claude mcp` / `/mcp` in an interactive session."}
